Implemented the reviewed Tix-to-CUDA lowering. The fixed API is exported from `dist/tensor/index.js` after build. [CUDA emission](src/tensor/cuda-source.ts) preserves statement and reduction order, including after `inline` and `split-sum`. The [checked pass](src/tensor/cuda-contract.ts) batches GPU cases and compares them against the current revision’s f64 evaluator, with the specified f32 fallback for nonfinite references.

**Framework changes:** none. The existing cross-kind transformation and asynchronous differential APIs were sufficient. [`tools/cuda-remote.mjs`](tools/cuda-remote.mjs) gained opt-in `--standalone` mode, which isolates each invocation’s files and shares compiled executables across input batches.

**Validation:** `npm run build` passed. `node --test tests/tensor/*.test.mjs` passed all 24 tests, including all six sampled corpus checks on the GB10, exact split-order checks, and rejection of a CUDA mutant that dropped a reduction term.

| Program | GB10 kernel median (ms) | Local f32 interpreter (s) |
|---|---:|---:|
| matmul | 0.229 | 514.487 |
| softmax | 0.463 | 38.215 |
| layernorm | 0.414 | 67.373 |
| attention | 0.890 | 313.957 |
| mlp | 0.968 | 871.406 |
| conv2d | 0.161 | 526.903 |

No lowering or contract deviations from the revised design. For measurement, matmul reports the median of three interpreter calls; the other programs use one full-size call each to limit shared-machine load. GPU measurements retain three same-process repetitions after preloading and warm-up. The [report](ttmp/2026/11/26/IRWB-022-F--lowering-tix-to-cuda-checked-on-the-gpu-machine/reference/02-cuda-lowering-results-and-corpus-timings.md) records the raw samples and methodology.

Commits: `a88d436` (review revisions), `d1d8a7e` (implementation), `9ff60d5` (validation and measurements). Working tree clean; not pushed.
